        "original_id": "f68c3965-0746-5133-9a51-d54a603b66f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jane Mayer, Charles Koch, David Koch, Steve Bannon, David Bossie\n- Organizations: Koch family, Koch Industries, Citizens United, Citizens United Productions\n- Products: Dark Money, Occupy Unmasked\n- Concepts: conservative libertarians, Occupy movement\n\nFacts:\n- Citizens United is a conservative 501(c)(4) nonprofit organization in the United States that was started in 1988 with major funding from the billionaire Koch family.\n- Koch Industries was the second-largest privately owned company in the United States, with 2013 revenues of $115 billion, and it was controlled by the Koch family.\n- Occupy Unmasked is a 2012 American documentary film directed by Steve Bannon, produced by David Bossie, and produced by Citizens United Productions.\n- Occupy Unmasked is critical of the Occupy movement.\n- Dark Money: The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right is a 2016 nonfiction book written by American investigative journalist Jane Mayer.\n- Dark Money says that extremely wealthy conservative libertarians, especially Charles Koch and David Koch, funded organizations that worked together to influence academic institutions, think tanks, courts, statehouses, Congress, and the American presidency for their own benefit.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8fa6e18a-4e6b-50a3-ab55-4afd6dac0b2c",
        "text": "Page: Dark Money (book). Sentence: Dark Money: The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right (2016) is a non-fiction book written by the American investigative journalist Jane Mayer, about a network of extremely wealthy conservative libertarians, foremost among them Charles and David Koch, who have together funded an array of organizations that work in tandem to influence academic institutions, think tanks, the courts, statehouses, Congress, and the American presidency for their own benefit.\nPage: Koch family. Sentence: The Koch family ( ) is an American family engaged in business, most noted for their political activities and control of Koch Industries, the second-largest privately owned company in the United States (with 2013 revenues of $115 billion).\nPage: Citizens United (organization). Sentence: Citizens United is a conservative 501(c)(4) non-profit organization in the United States started in 1988 with major funding from the billionaire Koch family.\nPage: Occupy Unmasked. Sentence: Occupy Unmasked is a 2012 American documentary film directed by Steve Bannon and produced by David Bossie, which is critical of the Occupy movement and was produced by Citizens United Productions.",
